    "content": "<!-- wp:cil/page-head {\"eyebrow\":\"2-Day Intensive One-to-One Circumcision Training Programme\",\"title\":\"Circumcision Training Course in London\",\"lede\":\"Beverley Clinic provides an intensive 2-day one-to-one circumcision training programme for doctors and appropriately qualified healthcare professionals who want to develop their knowledge and practical understanding of circumcision.\",\"crumbs\":[{\"label\":\"For doctors\",\"href\":\"\"}]} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section-sm\",\"band\":\"\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section-sm\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The programme combines circumcision theory, observation of live surgery, practical training using mannequins, complication management and guidance on establishing a circumcision service.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Because the course is delivered one-to-one, the teaching can be adapted to your existing experience, clinical background and areas you would particularly like to develop.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"cil-checklist\"} --><ul class=\"cil-checklist wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>2 days</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>One-to-one</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Live surgery</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Practical training</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Completion certificate</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:buttons {\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"margin\":{\"top\":\"24px\"}}}} --><div class=\"wp-block-buttons\" style=\"margin-top:24px\"><!-- wp:button --><div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"#enquire\">Enquire about training</a></div><!-- /wp:button --></div><!-- /wp:buttons --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-card edge\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"who-is-the-course-for\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-card edge\" id=\"who-is-the-course-for\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"heading\":\"Who Is the Course For?\",\"display\":\"d-2\",\"lede\":\"The circumcision training programme is designed for doctors and appropriately qualified healthcare professionals who want structured training in circumcision.\"} /--><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>It may be suitable for clinicians who:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"cil-checklist\"} --><ul class=\"cil-checklist wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Are new to circumcision</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Have some previous circumcision experience</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Want to improve their technique</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Want greater exposure to different circumcision methods</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Want to improve their understanding of complications</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Want to learn about circumcision across different age groups</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Are considering establishing or developing a circumcision service</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Before confirming training, we will ask about your professional qualifications, current role and previous circumcision experience so that the programme can be appropriately tailored.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-navy\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"why-one-to-one\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-navy\" id=\"why-one-to-one\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"heading\":\"Why One-to-One Circumcision Training?\",\"display\":\"d-2\",\"lede\":\"This is a bespoke one-to-one programme, rather than a large classroom course.\"} /--><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>This allows teaching to focus on your individual learning needs and provides more opportunity for discussion, questions and practical instruction.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The two days combine four main areas:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"columns\":\"g-4\",\"headingLevel\":3,\"items\":[{\"title\":\"Circumcision Theory \\u0026 Patient Assessment\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eUnderstand the anatomy, patient assessment, local anaesthesia, indications, contraindications and important abnormalities that should be recognised before circumcision.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Live Circumcision Observation\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eObserve live circumcision procedures performed in the clinic, with step-by-step explanation of the procedure and clinical decision-making.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Practical Circumcision Training\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003ePractise circumcision techniques, instrument handling and suturing using training mannequins.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Setting Up a Circumcision Service\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eLearn about the practical requirements involved in establishing and operating a circumcision service, including staffing, documentation, equipment, suppliers, indemnity and emergency arrangements.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"}]} /--></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-card edge\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"day-1\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-card edge\" id=\"day-1\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"heading\":\"Day 1 \u2013 Foundations, Plastibell \\u0026 Complications\",\"display\":\"d-2\",\"lede\":\"The first day concentrates on core circumcision theory, patient assessment, Plastibell circumcision and complication management.\"} /--><!-- wp:cil/split {\"reverse\":false} --><div class=\"wp-block-cil-split split\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading display d-3\"} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading display d-3\">Core Theory &amp; Patient Assessment</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Topics include:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"cil-checklist\"} --><ul class=\"cil-checklist wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Penile anatomy</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Nerve supply</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Blood supply</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Local anaesthetic</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Anatomical variations</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Penis size and shape</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Variations in skin distribution</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Indications for circumcision</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Contraindications to circumcision</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Patient selection and assessment</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Particular attention is given to recognising abnormalities that may alter whether or how circumcision should be performed.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>These include:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"cil-checklist\"} --><ul class=\"cil-checklist wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Hypospadias</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Chordee</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Bifid glans</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Hooded or incomplete foreskin</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Buried or concealed penis</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Recognising these findings before beginning a circumcision is an important part of safe clinical practice.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:cil/split --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"plastibell-and-live-observation\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section\" id=\"plastibell-and-live-observation\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/split {\"reverse\":false} --><div class=\"wp-block-cil-split split\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading display d-2\"} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading display d-2\">Plastibell Circumcision Training</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The programme covers the principles and practical steps involved in Plastibell circumcision.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Topics include:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"cil-checklist\"} --><ul class=\"cil-checklist wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Indications for Plastibell circumcision</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Selecting the appropriate Plastibell size</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Required instruments</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Preparation</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Step-by-step procedure</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Correct positioning of the device</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Aftercare</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Common parent questions</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Expected healing</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Plastibell separation</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Ring removal where required</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The aim is not simply to demonstrate the steps of the procedure, but to explain the clinical reasoning behind them.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading display d-2\"} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading display d-2\">Live Circumcision Observation</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Where suitable procedures are scheduled, you will have the opportunity to observe live circumcisions.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Procedures are explained step by step, including:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"cil-checklist\"} --><ul class=\"cil-checklist wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Patient assessment</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Preparation</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Local anaesthetic</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Instrument selection</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Procedural sequence</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Technique</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Immediate post-procedure assessment</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Aftercare</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The exact live cases available depend on the patients and procedures scheduled during the training dates and their clinical suitability for teaching.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:cil/split --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-card edge\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"practical-training\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-card edge\" id=\"practical-training\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"heading\":\"Practical Training\",\"display\":\"d-2\",\"lede\":\"You will have practical training using circumcision mannequins and instruments.\"} /--><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>This provides an opportunity to practise:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"cil-checklist\"} --><ul class=\"cil-checklist wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Plastibell technique</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Device selection</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Instrument handling</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Procedural sequencing</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Hand positioning</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Suturing</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Technique-related questions</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>One-to-one teaching allows practical sessions to be adapted according to your previous experience and progress.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-navy\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"circumcision-complications\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-navy\" id=\"circumcision-complications\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"heading\":\"Circumcision Complications\",\"display\":\"d-2\",\"lede\":\"An important part of Day 1 is understanding how complications occur and how they may be prevented or managed.\"} /--><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Training includes:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"columns\":\"g-3\",\"headingLevel\":3,\"items\":[{\"title\":\"Bleeding\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eUnderstanding potential causes of bleeding, prevention and approaches to management.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Excessive Skin Removal\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eHow excessive skin removal can occur and the importance of appropriate assessment and technique.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Insufficient Skin Removal\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eRecognising situations where too little skin has been removed and the possible consequences.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Constriction \\u0026 Scarring\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eUnderstanding circumferential scarring and constriction following circumcision.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Buried Penis\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eRecognising buried or concealed penis and understanding how anatomy affects circumcision planning and the amount of skin that should be removed.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"}]} /--><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\",\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"margin\":{\"top\":\"32px\"}}}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\" style=\"margin-top:32px\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Day 1 concludes with a recap and one-to-one question-and-answer session.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-warm\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"day-2\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-warm\" id=\"day-2\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"heading\":\"Day 2 \u2013 Forceps-Guided Circumcision, Special Cases \\u0026 Clinic Set-Up\",\"display\":\"d-2\",\"lede\":\"Day 2 develops the principles covered during Day 1 and focuses particularly on forceps-guided circumcision, different age groups, special cases, suturing and establishing a circumcision service.\"} /--><!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"columns\":\"g-2\",\"headingLevel\":3,\"items\":[{\"title\":\"Forceps-Guided Circumcision Training\",\"html\":\"<p>The course covers forceps-guided circumcision for:</p><ul class=\\\"cil-checklist\\\"><li>Babies</li><li>Children</li><li>Teenagers</li><li>Adults</li></ul><p>Teaching includes:</p><ul class=\\\"cil-checklist\\\"><li>Indications</li><li>Patient assessment</li><li>Instruments</li><li>Preparation</li><li>Procedural steps</li><li>Skin positioning</li><li>Haemostasis</li><li>Suturing</li><li>Wound management</li><li>Aftercare</li><li>Common patient and parent questions</li></ul><p>A freehand circumcision technique may also be discussed and demonstrated during live teaching where appropriate.</p>\"},{\"title\":\"Circumcision Styles\",\"html\":\"<p>Training includes discussion of different circumcision outcomes and the factors that influence them.</p><p>This includes:</p><ul class=\\\"cil-checklist\\\"><li>High circumcision</li><li>Low circumcision</li><li>Tight circumcision</li><li>Loose circumcision</li><li>Anatomical limitations</li><li>Patient expectations</li><li>Safe skin removal</li></ul><p>The emphasis is on understanding how anatomy and technique influence the final result rather than simply applying the same approach to every patient.</p>\"}]} /--></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"therapeutic-and-special-cases\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section\" id=\"therapeutic-and-special-cases\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"heading\":\"Therapeutic \\u0026 Special Circumcision Cases\",\"display\":\"d-2\",\"lede\":\"The programme also covers clinical considerations when circumcision is being performed because of a foreskin problem.\"} /--><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Topics include:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"columns\":\"g-3\",\"headingLevel\":3,\"items\":[{\"title\":\"Phimosis\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eAssessment and circumcision considerations in patients with a tight or scarred foreskin.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Paraphimosis\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eUnderstanding paraphimosis and the considerations surrounding subsequent circumcision.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Balanitis\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eCircumcision considerations in patients with recurrent inflammation affecting the foreskin and glans.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Re-Circumcision\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eAssessment and planning where a patient has previously been circumcised and requires revision.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Frenulum Treatment\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eAssessment of the frenulum and circumstances in which frenulum treatment may be required alongside circumcision.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"}]} /--></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-card edge\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"live-surgery-and-hands-on\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-card edge\" id=\"live-surgery-and-hands-on\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"heading\":\"Live Surgery \\u0026 Hands-On Training\",\"display\":\"d-2\",\"lede\":\"Day 2 can include further observation of live circumcision procedures, depending on the cases scheduled during the training dates.\"} /--><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Practical mannequin training includes:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"cil-checklist\"} --><ul class=\"cil-checklist wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Forceps-guided circumcision</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Instrument handling</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Procedural sequencing</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Suturing techniques</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Wound closure</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Questions about technique and troubleshooting</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The one-to-one format allows additional time to be spent on areas where you would particularly like to improve.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-navy\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"setting-up-a-clinic\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-navy\" id=\"setting-up-a-clinic\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"heading\":\"Setting Up a Circumcision Clinic\",\"display\":\"d-2\",\"lede\":\"Knowing how to perform a procedure is only one part of providing a circumcision service.\"} /--><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The programme therefore includes practical guidance about establishing and running a circumcision clinic.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Topics include:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"columns\":\"g-3\",\"headingLevel\":3,\"items\":[{\"title\":\"Clinic \\u0026 Staffing\",\"html\":\"\\u003cul\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eClinic requirements\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eRecruitment\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eStaff roles\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eStaff training\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003ePatient flow\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003c/ul\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Documentation\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eDiscussion of the documentation required for a circumcision service, including:\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cul\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003ePatient information\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eConsent documentation\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eClinical documentation\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eAftercare information\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eTemplates used within a circumcision service\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003c/ul\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Equipment \\u0026 Instruments\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eGuidance on:\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cul\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eCircumcision instruments\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eEquipment\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eConsumables\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003ePlastibell supplies\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eClinic equipment\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eSuppliers\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003c/ul\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Professional \\u0026 Emergency Arrangements\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eDiscussion includes:\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cul\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eProfessional indemnity\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eEmergency cover\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003eAppropriate clinical arrangements\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003cli\\u003ePlanning for complications\\u003c/li\\u003e\\u003c/ul\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Developing Your Service\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eWe also discuss practical considerations involved in developing a circumcision service, including clinic organisation and website considerations.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"}]} /--></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-card edge\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"what-is-included\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-card edge\" id=\"what-is-included\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"heading\":\"What Is Included in the Training?\",\"display\":\"d-2\"} /--><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The 2-day programme includes:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"cil-checklist\"} --><ul class=\"cil-checklist wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>One-to-one training</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Circumcision theory</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Penile anatomy</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Patient assessment</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Local anaesthetic</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Recognition of important penile abnormalities</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Plastibell circumcision</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Forceps-guided circumcision</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Overview of freehand circumcision</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Live procedure observation where suitable cases are available</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Practical mannequin training</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Circumcision instruments</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Suturing</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Complication prevention and management</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Buried penis considerations</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Circumcision styles</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Medical and therapeutic circumcision</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Re-circumcision</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Frenulum treatment</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Aftercare</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Patient and parent communication</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Clinic set-up</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Documentation and templates</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Equipment and suppliers</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Indemnity and emergency cover</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>One-to-one questions and discussion</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Certificate of completion</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"live-cases\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section\" id=\"live-cases\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/split {\"reverse\":false} --><div class=\"wp-block-cil-split split\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading display d-2\"} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading display d-2\">What Live Cases Will I See?</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Live cases depend on the procedures scheduled during your training dates and whether those cases are clinically appropriate for teaching.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Cases may include circumcision of:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"cil-checklist\"} --><ul class=\"cil-checklist wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Babies</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Children</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Teenagers</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Adults</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Because patient care and suitability come first, we cannot guarantee that every age group or every type of procedure will be available during a particular course.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Theoretical and mannequin teaching is used to ensure that the programme still covers the core techniques.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading display d-2\"} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading display d-2\">Will I Perform Circumcision on Live Patients?</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The programme includes observation of live circumcision procedures and practical hands-on training using circumcision mannequins.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We do not guarantee that a delegate will independently perform circumcision on a live patient during the course.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The priority is patient safety, appropriate consent and ensuring that any involvement in clinical care is suitable for the individual circumstances.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:cil/split --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-warm\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"more-than-the-procedure\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-warm\" id=\"more-than-the-procedure\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"heading\":\"More Than Learning the Procedure\",\"display\":\"d-2\",\"lede\":\"Circumcision training should involve more than learning how to remove the foreskin.\"} /--><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>A clinician also needs to understand:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"cil-checklist\"} --><ul class=\"cil-checklist wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Who is suitable for circumcision</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>When circumcision should not proceed</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>How anatomy affects technique</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>How much skin can safely be removed</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>How to recognise important abnormalities</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>How to achieve haemostasis</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>How to manage the wound</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>How to recognise and respond to complications</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>What aftercare patients and parents require</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>How to organise a safe circumcision service</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>These principles are integrated throughout both days of the programme.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-navy\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"why-train-with-us\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-navy\" id=\"why-train-with-us\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"heading\":\"Why Train at Beverley Clinic?\",\"display\":\"d-2\"} /--><!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"columns\":\"g-3\",\"headingLevel\":3,\"items\":[{\"title\":\"Circumcision is a core part of our clinical work\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eCircumcision is part of our regular day-to-day clinical practice.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eOur experience includes circumcision across different age groups and a range of anatomical and clinical presentations.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Training based on real clinical practice\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eThe course combines theory with live clinical observation and practical training, allowing teaching to be connected to the realities of providing circumcision care.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"One-to-one teaching\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eThe programme is delivered individually rather than to a large group.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eThis allows more time for questions and enables the course to be adapted to your experience and learning objectives.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"All-age circumcision experience\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eOur clinical work includes babies, children, teenagers and adults, allowing the programme to explore how circumcision changes across different age groups.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"title\":\"Practical clinic experience\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eThe course goes beyond surgical technique and includes the practical considerations involved in setting up and operating a circumcision service.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"}]} /--></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-card edge\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"certificate\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-card edge\" id=\"certificate\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"heading\":\"Certificate of Completion\",\"display\":\"d-2\",\"lede\":\"A certificate of completion is provided after completing the 2-day training programme.\"} /--><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The certificate confirms participation in and completion of the course.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Completion of the course does not automatically constitute independent professional accreditation or confirmation that a clinician is competent to practise circumcision independently.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Each clinician remains responsible for ensuring that they practise within their professional scope, competence, registration requirements and indemnity arrangements.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/faq {\"heading\":\"Frequently Asked Questions\",\"items\":[{\"q\":\"How long is the circumcision training course?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eThe programme takes place over two intensive days.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Is the training one-to-one?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eYes. The programme is delivered one-to-one, allowing the teaching to be tailored to your experience and learning requirements.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Does the course include live circumcision?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eThe course includes observation of live circumcision procedures where suitable cases are scheduled and appropriate for teaching.\\u003c/p\\u003e \\u003cp\\u003eThe exact case mix cannot be guaranteed in advance.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Which circumcision techniques are covered?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eThe programme covers Plastibell circumcision and forceps-guided circumcision, together with an overview of freehand circumcision where appropriate.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Does the course cover babies and adults?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eYes. The programme discusses circumcision across different age groups, including babies, children and adults.\\u003c/p\\u003e \\u003cp\\u003eLive case availability depends on the procedures scheduled during the training dates.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Is there practical training?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eYes. Practical training is carried out using circumcision mannequins and instruments and includes procedural technique and suturing.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Does the course cover circumcision complications?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eYes. Complication prevention, recognition and management form an important part of the programme.\\u003c/p\\u003e \\u003cp\\u003eTopics include bleeding, excessive or insufficient skin removal, scarring, constriction and buried penis.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Does the course cover setting up a circumcision clinic?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eYes. We discuss staffing, documentation, consent, equipment, instruments, suppliers, indemnity, emergency arrangements and other practical aspects of establishing a circumcision service.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Will I receive a certificate?\",\"a\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eYes. A certificate of completion is provided following completion of the 2-day programme.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"}]} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"enquire\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section\" id=\"enquire\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/split {\"reverse\":false} --><div class=\"wp-block-cil-split split\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading display d-2\"} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading display d-2\">Enquire About Circumcision Training</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If you are interested in attending our 2-day one-to-one circumcision training programme, please contact Beverley Clinic.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>When enquiring, it is helpful to tell us:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"cil-checklist\"} --><ul class=\"cil-checklist wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Your full name</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Your professional role</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Your qualifications</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Where you currently work</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Your previous circumcision experience</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Circumcision techniques you already use, if applicable</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Areas you would particularly like to develop</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Your preferred training dates</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>This allows us to understand your experience and tailor the programme appropriately.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:buttons {\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"margin\":{\"top\":\"24px\"}}}} --><div class=\"wp-block-buttons\" style=\"margin-top:24px\"><!-- wp:button --><div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"#courses\">Enquire about circumcision training</a></div><!-- /wp:button --><!-- wp:button {\"className\":\"is-style-outline\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"/contact/\">Contact Beverley Clinic</a></div><!-- /wp:button --></div><!-- /wp:buttons --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:cil/callback-card {\"eyebrow\":\"Course enquiry\",\"title\":\"Ask about dates\",\"formId\":\"courses\",\"subject\":\"training course enquiry\",\"urgent\":false} /--></div><!-- /wp:cil/split --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->",
    "seo": {
        "document_title": "Circumcision Training Course UK | 2-Day Intensive Training",
        "meta_description": "2-day intensive one-to-one circumcision training for doctors and healthcare professionals in London. Theory, live surgery observation, practical training, complications and clinic set-up."
    }
}
